# bat's colours are the terminal's palette (ghostty/themes/OneDark): the theme maps each
# token role to a slot the way One Dark assigns them (keywords magenta, functions blue,
# strings green, numbers orange, comments grey), see themes/ansi-roles.tmTheme. delta
# reads the same theme for diffs, and the fzf and hints previews get it through here.
# bat loads custom themes from its cache: run `bat cache --build` once after stow, and
# again after a bat upgrade (bat says when the cache is stale).
--theme="ansi-roles"

# Comments are italic in the theme, as they are on the command line; bat drops italics
# unless told the terminal shows them.
--italic-text=always
